        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(nodes-camera): add timeout to URL media downloads",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nNode camera URL-backed media downloads used the guarded fetch path but did not provide a request deadline. If the node host accepted the connection and never sent headers or completed the response, `writeUrlToFile` could wait indefinitely while saving camera artifacts.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\nThis PR adds a 120s deadline to `writeUrlToFile`'s guarded fetch call, while leaving the existing HTTPS requirement, node-host match, redirect host validation, body cleanup, and max-byte enforcement intact. Tests can pass a smaller timeout override so the regression proof remains fast.\n\n## User Impact\nA stalled node-hosted camera URL now fails through the existing error path instead of wedging the CLI media write.\n\n## Evidence\n- Focused test: `pnpm vitest run src/cli/nodes-camera.test.ts` -> 29 passed.\n- Format/lint: `pnpm exec oxfmt --check --threads=1 src/cli/nodes-camera.ts src/cli/nodes-camera.test.ts && pnpm exec oxlint src/cli/nodes-camera.ts src/cli/nodes-camera.test.ts && git diff --check` -> passed.\n- Whitespace: `git diff --check` -> clean.\n- Collision check before opening: open PR changed-files query for `src/cli/nodes-camera.ts` returned no open PRs.\n\n## Proof\nRegression contract: the branch test `aborts hanging url payload downloads through the guarded fetch timeout` starts a local `node:http` server that accepts the request and never sends response headers. It then calls `writeUrlToFile` with a production-shaped HTTPS node URL, routes the guarded fetch mock to that real hanging server, asserts `timeoutMs: 50`, and verifies the expected output path is missing after the failure.\n\nControlled stall transcript from the same guarded fetch runtime path, using a 500ms timeout so the proof does not wait two minutes:\n\n```text\n$ pnpm exec tsx --input-type=module - <<'SCRIPT'\n# starts a local node:http server, calls fetchWithSsrFGuard with timeoutMs=500,\n# and lets the server accept the request while withholding headers\nSCRIPT\nstall-server: accepted node media request; intentionally withholding headers\n[fetch-timeout] fetch timeout after 500ms (elapsed 501ms) operation=fetchWithSsrFGuard url=http://127.0.0.1:<port>/camera.bin\nguarded-fetch: aborted stalled request after 585ms\nguarded-fetch: error=TimeoutError: request timed out\n```\n\nWhy this covers the bug: before this PR, `writeUrlToFile` did not pass a request timeout into `fetchWithSsrFGuard`, so a node-hosted URL that accepted the connection but withheld headers could remain pending. After this PR, the same guarded fetch path has a deadline; the committed regression also asserts no partial output file is left behind.\n\nCompatibility note: the production deadline is intentionally 120s total for URL-backed camera media downloads. A node-hosted transfer that is still progressing but takes longer than 120s can now fail instead of hanging indefinitely.\n\nWhat was not tested: live node hardware. The proof uses a controlled local hanging server plus the committed `writeUrlToFile` regression.\n",
